  "content": "# Binary Search and `lower_bound`\n\n## The Big Idea: Binary Search\n\nImagine you're looking up a name in a **physical phone book**. You wouldn't start at page 1 and flip one page at a time. Instead, you'd open it roughly in the middle, see whether the name you want comes before or after the current page, and then **throw away half the book**. You repeat this, halving the search space each time, until you find your name.\n\nThat's binary search: **repeatedly halving the search space** by comparing your target to the middle element.\n\n> \ufffd",
